                            {
                                "target_word": "rip",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ea22e931-b106-3d87-87c7-6694cdb7961f",
                                        "entry_id": "1bea9e14-b864-3c59-bc4c-68bb304dcad8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To divide or separate the parts of (especially something flimsy, such as paper or fabric), by cutting or tearing; to tear off or out by violence."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f3ea2cf0-bd59-4046-b5e1-119f006da1a9",
                                                "sense_id": "ea22e931-b106-3d87-87c7-6694cdb7961f",
                                                "text": "to rip a garment; to rip up a floor"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "28402843-b499-4ccc-b9b4-e60b086613ac",
                                                "sense_id": "ea22e931-b106-3d87-87c7-6694cdb7961f",
                                                "text": "For a spell we done pretty well. Then there came a reg'lar terror of a sou'wester same as you don't get one summer in a thousand, and blowed the shanty flat and ripped about half of the weir poles out of the sand."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "accaaa59-2666-491a-9e92-631441d6ff67",
                                                "sense_id": "ea22e931-b106-3d87-87c7-6694cdb7961f",
                                                "text": "A canister of flour from the kitchen had been thrown at the looking-glass and lay like trampled snow over the remains of a decent blue suit with the lining ripped out which lay on top of the ruin of a plastic wardrobe."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0b5a4ed9-6fdf-407c-ae64-6db7df07d9bc",
                                                "sense_id": "ea22e931-b106-3d87-87c7-6694cdb7961f",
                                                "text": "On the other hand, HMS Colossus takes multiple hits from several battleships at once, having drifted closer to the German fleet than the rest of her squadron. She explodes as multiple magazine detonations rip the ship apart, and is lost with all hands."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d9b3ee00-0538-3fff-baac-6e444cab0f26",
                                        "entry_id": "1bea9e14-b864-3c59-bc4c-68bb304dcad8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To tear apart; to rapidly become two parts."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9c4e3d9d-e948-4b68-94b8-aaf3f3d2b1b2",
                                                "sense_id": "d9b3ee00-0538-3fff-baac-6e444cab0f26",
                                                "text": "My shirt ripped when it was caught on a bramble."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "27205adc-1113-3755-867a-0c36ceed8f17",
                                        "entry_id": "1bea9e14-b864-3c59-bc4c-68bb304dcad8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To remove violently or wrongly."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b1f75805-3e8a-42f5-9a98-8b4258120ed7",
                                                "sense_id": "27205adc-1113-3755-867a-0c36ceed8f17",
                                                "text": "A child untimely ripped from its parents' arms."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6d727bc9-3c99-47ad-92a8-fd33ec5c127e",
                                                "sense_id": "27205adc-1113-3755-867a-0c36ceed8f17",
                                                "text": "Mary is sister to the marginalized women who live unchronicled lives in oppressive situations. It does her no honor to rip her out of her conflictual, dangerous historical circumstances and transmute her into an icon of a peaceful, middle-class life robed in royal blue."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fa0a2d7a-f1a0-3f44-b623-2f60fe24fa14",
                                        "entry_id": "1bea9e14-b864-3c59-bc4c-68bb304dcad8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To get by, or as if by, cutting or tearing."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "84035b24-c8f7-45fb-b70f-c96a242c08c7",
                                                "sense_id": "fa0a2d7a-f1a0-3f44-b623-2f60fe24fa14",
                                                "text": "He'll rip the fatal secret from her heart."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1705c6f1-099a-3983-b7e8-28b2520f3003",
                                        "entry_id": "1bea9e14-b864-3c59-bc4c-68bb304dcad8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To move quickly and destructively."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "356c7837-0cf8-4eb5-b57a-82f70efd8a8b",
                                                "sense_id": "1705c6f1-099a-3983-b7e8-28b2520f3003",
                                                "text": "“Wall,” said the landlord, fetching a long breath, “that’s a purty long sarmon for a chap that rips a little now and then. ...\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7b8896f3-442d-4e31-8cf0-4151ca98126e",
                                                "sense_id": "1705c6f1-099a-3983-b7e8-28b2520f3003",
                                                "text": "On 18 November 1987 a horrific flash fire ripped through the escalators and ticket hall of King's Cross tube station, killing thirty people."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "00eb4eb3-e7fb-3f0a-8937-5d71510a99dd",
                                        "entry_id": "1bea9e14-b864-3c59-bc4c-68bb304dcad8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To cut wood along (parallel to) the grain."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c0889235-1934-397c-b924-a04dd4be3d2e",
                                        "entry_id": "1bea9e14-b864-3c59-bc4c-68bb304dcad8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To copy data from a CD, DVD, Internet stream, etc., to a hard drive, portable device, etc."
                                        ],
